+- **The constant.** `SRP_REDECLARE_CS` (`srp_mbx.c`) is twice `SRP_LEAVEALL_LONGEST_CS` less the JoinTime and (`CTRL_LOOP_TX_MS` + 9) / 10: 2,977 cs at 1x1/1if, 2,973 at 8x8/1if and 2,970 at two interfaces (#951: 3,023, 3,027 and 3,030). The count still starts at the Leave's request. On the model's wire, with the request on a centisecond, the changed destination is declared 29,770 ms after it at 1x1/1if (29,700 at 8x8/2if), and with the loop held a JoinTime and THE TRANSMIT's figure from the tick that ends the count it leaves at 29,995 ms at both, under the 30,000 the two periods give (`srp_talker.cpp`). `declare_sources` keeps its size: 2,977 needs the same `lui` and `addi` as 3,023. That held first only where lwSRP's join timer was idle as the count ended. With it running, at withdrawals 270 to 340 ms into a second of the participants' periodic MRPDUs at 1x1/1if, 310 to 380 at 8x8/1if and 340 to 410 at 8x8/2if, the held loop's changed destination waited for the next periodic MRPDU, 30.6 to 30.7 s after the request (the sliced build, below). At every phase, each centisecond of a second, with the loop held or serviced and the join timer idle or running, it now leaves no sooner than the count's end and, held, at 29,995 ms at 1x1/1if and 8x8/2if and 29,997 at 8x8/1if (`EveryPhase/TalkerPhase.*`, and `Talker.ChangedDestinationReachesTheWireWithinTwoLongestLeaveAllPeriodsWithTheJoinTimerRunning` at 340 ms, run at all three).
+- **The record.** lwSRP indicates every Listener registration's start and end, Ignore at the end, and every change of a registered Listener's declaration, so `listener` records each change of the declaration it copies, while the source's DA gate is open on the interface, in `noticed`, the record a Talker declaration's change is (#936), and the composition and AECP take it the same way. MAAP opens a source's gate on its own interface only, and behind a closed gate the face shows neither flag, so a Listener on another interface, or behind a closed gate, records nothing. A reset of the interface destroys its participants and their registrations with no indication, so `reset_interface` clears each source's declaration with `listener_present`: the record agrees with the answer, no Listener, and the first registration after it is recorded whatever it declares, the destroyed one's declaration included (`Talker.ListenerRegistrationAfterAResetIsNoticed`, `AppOutputs.ListenerRegistrationAfterALinkResetIsItsStreamOutputsNotice`).
+- **The sliced build.** THE TRANSMIT builds an interface's two MRPDUs in two slices at every point (`CTRL_LOOP_BUILD_MOST` 1). The pass the count's end owes declares the changed destination and builds the MSRP MRPDU, which lwSRP's join timer holds when a periodic MRPDU left in the JoinTime before it; the timer's end, among the centiseconds a held loop dispatches before the build's second slice, set the interface's due again. That due was set already, and the second slice's end cleared it, so the declaration waited for the next periodic MRPDU. The pause now takes the interface's due, the build waiting for its next slice is THE TRANSMIT's due and the poll's owed (`tx_owed`, the due and `tx_resume` read whole in one load), and what came due since its first slice is owed again once the build ends: a pass, as after a build made whole, and none when nothing came due, what its own sends moved included; a frame the ring refuses in the second slice stays the poll's with its interface due (A3), as in a build made whole (`Srp.ABuildPausedBetweenSlicesStaysOwedAndKeepsWhatCameDue`; plants `build-paused-*` and `build-resumed-drops-what-came-due` in `srp_transmit_mutants.py`, `talker-resume-*` in `srp_talker_mutants.py`).
+- **The rom it fits in.** The target platform's 8x8 image at one interface, a product image, had 56 bytes of its 34 RAMB36 of `rom` left at the flip train's head (139,208 of 139,264 B; `plat_ledger.py`). A comparison of what the output shows at each copy, with a record and a delivery loop of its own, added 296 bytes at 8x8/1if and put the CPU budget harness's `declaring-outputs` image there over its 32 RAMB36; a second form, 152 bytes, put the platform's image over its ledgered 58 RAMB36. This one adds 40 bytes, all in `listener` (128 to 168 B at 8x8/1if, 132 to 172 at 1x1): 139,248 B, 16 left. The corrections that follow review add 4 bytes in `reset_interface` for the clear, and `transmit_aged` and the poll keep their sizes, reading `tx_owed` in one load (reading the two bytes apart took 16 more, and that form put the image over its 58 RAMB36, 139,280 B). In `transmit` the kept due took 12 more and filled the rom, 139,264 B; at one interface the build's interface is now 0 at compile time, as it always was there, so `transmit` is 112 bytes smaller there with the kept due and the refused slice's due: 139,136 B, 128 left. No budget moved. Each source's declaration is held beside the interface's other per-source byte arrays, so `struct ctrl_plat` keeps its ledgered size at every point (`ctrl_memory_ledger.py`, `PLAT_*`).
+- **The images.** At base and head: the target platform's four, the size fixture's four and the CPU budget harness's twelve. At 1x1 `srp_mbx.o` alone differs. At 8x8 the declarations' array moves the interface's later fields 8 bytes, so `ctrl_app_aecp.o`, `ctrl_app_srp.o` and `ctrl_plat.o` (the fixture's `ctrl_aecp_image.o`) differ in those offsets alone, no function's size with them. `plat_ledger.py` passes at every point. The release (all-fabric) image is byte-identical but for LiteX's generation times and the CPU netlist's per-run name. The corrections, `0d80f0ed` (its images `8845364d`'s) against `b4a1dde2`: in each of the target platform's and the size fixture's images `srp_mbx.o` alone differs, `transmit` 116 bytes smaller at 1x1/1if and 112 at 8x8/1if, 40 larger at 1x1/2if and 36 at 8x8/2if, and `reset_interface` 4 larger at 8x8, the same at 1x1. `plat_ledger.py` passes at every point, `rom` 126,360, 128,112, 139,136 and 140,864 B, and the CPU budget harness's images, every arm at its three points, link within their budgets. The release image is again byte-identical but for those and LiteX's per-run order of the CPU ISA string's extensions, which the same revision exported again also changes.
 
 - **The rows.** Measured base against head on the legs the change's code runs in and those its placement may move, at 1x1/1if and 8x8/1if: arm A's `srp`, `backlog-owed`, `aecp` and `datapath-events` (and `aecp-largest-notice` at 1x1/1if), the `valid-destinations` arm's `srp-talker-held`, a Listener Ready for every source, so `listener` records each, and `srp-talker-loss`, and the `declaring-outputs` arm's `aecp-outputs`, whose output 0's Listener Ready is now its own notice. No probe changes its verdict, each side has arm A's seven `backlog-owed` misses and no other, and no pass is over the share. Every stated cost measured is within by the rule but one, restated: 8x8/1if's own MAAP record measures 17,259 cycles in `srp-talker-loss` (16,176 on the base in the same group), 185 us by the rule over its 180, so `load_grade.OWN` states 185. `flip_grade.py --check` and `load_grade.py --check` still pass at 8x8/1if: its load 0.744 of 0.75, and THE TRANSMIT's row by every source 76.86 ms of its 77 (76.81 at 180). The record runs none of the change's code: the 8 bytes each 8x8 interface's SRP state grew move the data after it, and at 1x1, where nothing grew, it measures the same on both. The SRP record's apply, where `listener` runs, grows most: `record.srp` 23,456 to 24,266 cycles at 1x1/1if, 255 of its 285 us. `centisecond` measures 16,064 there, 170 of its 170 us (15,672 on the base in the same group). The `declaring-outputs` arm now expects output 0's Listener notice to every registration after the declared Talker's (`declaring_outputs.order_findings`, three planted orders refused). This is a sample, not the formal measurement: the other groups and arms were not run.
+- **The rows after the corrections.** The same legs, round 1's head runs (images `0d80f0ed`'s) against `b4a1dde2`'s, at 1x1/1if and 8x8/1if, with the formal measurement's options. No probe changes its verdict, 71 and 95 paired, each side has arm A's seven `backlog-owed` misses and no other, and no pass is over the share. Every stated cost measured is within by the rule, 66 at 1x1/1if and 66 at 8x8/1if; at its statement, as before, only `item.acmp_declined` at both points, and at 8x8/1if `record.srp`, 35,507 cycles in `srp-talker-held`, 375 of its 375 us (35,273 before, also 375). THE TRANSMIT's passes: no pass makes both MRPDUs (each slice holds one), a build of one is at most 52,531 CPU cycles at 1x1/1if (53,168 before; 735 us stated) and 126,644 in `srp-talker-held` at 8x8/1if (125,209 before; 1,475 us stated), no MRPDU a timer owes is late, and the join timers' MRPDUs are 187.2 to 190.6 ms apart. 1x1/1if's centisecond measures 14,213 cycles, 150 of its 170 us (16,064 before, 170 of 170), and 8x8/1if's own MAAP record 17,014 cycles in `srp-talker-loss`, 180 of its 185 us (17,259 before, 185). No statement or bound changes, so `flip_grade.py --check` at both points, `load_grade.py --check` and `shape_costs.py --check` pass as before, THE TRANSMIT's row by every source 76.86 ms of its 77 at 8x8/1if. This is a sample, not the formal measurement.
 
